-> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66 (matches `test_half_even`).\n\n## Notes\nThis changes rounding behavior for any caller relying on half-up semantics. Worth a look from payments reviewers before merge.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 400771, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013rSrVLHHWFFuSRwjXuQiE5", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 400771, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013rSrVLHHWFFuSRwjXuQiE5", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 402191, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014cRrx3puoBdxaSMmZvcFuw", "tool": "request_review", "args": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 402491, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014cRrx3puoBdxaSMmZvcFuw", "tool": "request_review", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 402491, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014cRrx3puoBdxaSMmZvcFuw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 404183, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The nightly failure is fixed, CI passes, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` expect banker's rounding per FIN-212. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). The first open call returned an empty reviewers list, so I sent a separate review request to alex, which succeeded.\n\nThis changes rounding for any caller that relied on half-up, so the PR description flags it for reviewers. I did not merge; merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the two files and the ticket reference.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012sGhrpsNMJ6edUB473obwZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015MUaU8aXfKYyFpUj3jBXqD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CGvSax4j2iTYY4MqjPV8tq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and the test expect `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Under half-even, 2.675 \u2192 2.68 (7 is odd, so round to the even 8) and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 (6 is already even), which matches the test. I'll create the branch and make the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CUbJ9xUXneUhZj4e6D16cN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VzR2NuqGkCUjmRpp71Mxgq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012wLnzntzAPSvFDU8M2EikA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GttCxkyXXTFwpZBifzzgzN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013rSrVLHHWFFuSRwjXuQiE5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Summary\nNightly build of payments-service was failing because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updates the import accordingly. The function's docstring already described banker's rounding, so the code now matches it.\n\n## Verification\n- CI run `ci-0001` passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- Examples: 2.675 -> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66 (matches `test_half_even`).\n\n## Notes\nThis changes rounding behavior for any caller relying on half-up semantics. Worth a look from payments reviewers before merge.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but the response shows an empty reviewers list, so the review request may not have registered. I'll request review from alex explicitly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014cRrx3puoBdxaSMmZvcFuw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed, CI passes, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Fix:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` expect banker's rounding per FIN-212. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). The first open call returned an empty reviewers list, so I sent a separate review request to alex, which succeeded.\n\nThis changes rounding for any caller that relied on half-up, so the PR description flags it for reviewers. I did not merge; merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}